{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Ring.Defs","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.BigOperators.Ring.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring"],"declarations":4,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.extra_rows_tradeoff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.extra_rows_tradeoff","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RoundedWaterfillExchange.lean#L139-L146","doc":"**Extra rows.** `j` rows beyond `k` gain `j A` and cost at least `(L/2) j (j − 1)` of hook\nenergy; the net is at most `(A + L/2)²/(2L)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.diagonal_exchange","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.diagonal_exchange","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RoundedWaterfillExchange.lean#L101-L137","doc":"**Diagonal exchange.** Let `a d` (cells of a shape on anti-diagonal `d`) and `o d` (the greedy\nfill: full diagonals up to `k`, partial at `k+1`, empty beyond) have the same total, with\n`a d ≤ o d` for `d ≤ k` and `o d = 0` for `d ≥ k + 2`. Then the weighted excess is at least the\ncost of the cells beyond diagonal `k + 1`:\n`Σ (a d − o d)·d ≥ Σ_{d ≥ k+2} a d · (d − k − 1)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.int_tradeoff","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.int_tradeoff","kind":"theorem","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RoundedWaterfillExchange.lean#L80-L99","doc":"**Per-coordinate trade-off on the integer grid.** For `x ∈ ℕ`, a gain `ω x` against the\ndiscrete energy `(L/2)(x² − x)` is at most `ω + ω²/(2L)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.rounded_pythagoras","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.RoundedWaterfillExchange.rounded_pythagoras","kind":"theorem","line":41,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidKnot/RoundedWaterfillExchange.lean#L41-L78","doc":"**Discrete (rounded water-fill) Pythagoras.** If every `q i ≥ a`, every coordinate where\n`t` lies strictly below `q` has `q i ≤ a + 1`, and the sums agree, then\n`Σ q² + Σ (t − q)² − Σ |t − q| ≤ Σ t²`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}